     <string name="doris_core_layout_description">Which CPU cores the heavy emulator threads use. Doris puts the GPU emulation thread, the busiest one, on the fastest core and keeps the other heavy threads on the middle cores, so they never slow each other down. Takes effect the next time the game starts.</string>
     <string name="doris_cores_doris">Doris: GPU thread on the fastest core</string>
     <string name="doris_cores_system">Let Android decide (Eden)</string>
-    <string name="doris_texture_gc">Texture memory cleanup</string>
-    <string name="doris_texture_gc_description">When the texture cache throws out old textures. Eden starts at 1.6 GB of GPU memory, which TotK always uses, so it removes and re-uploads thousands of textures every few seconds, and for textures the GPU drew into it either waits for the GPU (a hitch) or loses the drawing (flicker). Doris starts at 2.4 GB, waits longer, and keeps GPU drawings unless memory is critical. Takes effect right away.</string>
-    <string name="doris_texture_gc_doris">Doris: keep GPU drawings, clean up later</string>
-    <string name="doris_texture_gc_eden">Eden (as before)</string>
     <string name="doris_gpu_barriers">GPU barriers</string>
     <string name="doris_gpu_barriers_description">How the game\'s \"wait until the GPU is done\" points are carried out. Eden\'s way lets later drawing read results that aren\'t finished yet on Adreno, which can make distant terrain, buildings and shadows drop out for a frame. Doris uses real barriers. Takes effect the next time the game starts.</string>
     <string name="doris_barriers_eden">Eden (as before)</string>
